#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/aligned_alloc.3:91
msgid ""
"I<size> had to be a multiple of I<alignment>.  Otherwise, the behavior was "
"undefined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/aligned_alloc.3:96
msgid "If I<alignment> was not a power of two, the behavior was undefined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/aligned_alloc.3:103
msgid ""
"E<.UR "
"https:\\://www.open-std.org/\\:jtc1/\\:sc22/\\:wg14/\\:www/\\:docs/\\:summary.htm#dr_460> "
"DR460 E<.UE> reported both cases of UB as unnecessarily dangerous, and fixed "
"them with a Technical Corrigendum that transformed them into errors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/aligned_alloc.3:114
msgid ""
"E<.UR "
"https:\\://www.open-std.org/\\:jtc1/\\:sc22/\\:wg14/\\:www/\\:docs/\\:n2072.htm> "
"N2072 E<.UE> reported that the requirement that I<size> is a multiple of "
"I<alignment> is superfluous, and removed it with a Technical Corrigendum."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/aligned_alloc.3:117
msgid ""
"C17 incorporates both technical corrigenda.  The API has been stable since "
"C17."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/aligned_alloc.3:124
msgid ""
"glibc initially implemented it as silently aligning as "
"I<stdc_bit_ceil(alignment)> instead of I<alignment>.  Since glibc 2.38, it "
"implements the C17 specification."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/aligned_alloc.3:129
msgid ""
"Some implementations, such as FreeBSD/jemalloc, implement the C17 "
"specification, even though their documentation claims having undefined "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/aligned_alloc.3:134
msgid ""
"Some implementations, such as OpenBSD, implement C11 amended with DR460, "
"even though their documentation claims having undefined behavior."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/aligned_alloc.3:139
msgid ""
"No known implementations have exploited the undefined behavior in a more "
"dangerous way.  This function should be safe to use."
msgstr ""

