#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/aligned_alloc.3:148
msgid ""
"On many systems there are alignment restrictions, for example, on buffers "
"used for direct block device I/O.  POSIX specifies the "
"I<pathconf(path,_PC_REC_XFER_ALIGN)> call that tells what alignment is "
"needed.  Now one can use B<aligned_alloc>()  to satisfy this requirement."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/aligned_alloc.3:154
msgid ""
"The glibc B<malloc>(3)  always returns 8-byte aligned memory addresses, so "
"this function is needed only if you require larger alignment values."
msgstr ""

